{"c":[{"id":"5ac6125c74b45908","sum":"G2-P2: never widen restates(); guest fixture at x=0; say 'at 3pm'; no default chat route. Page plans set WindowSel.page, page focus from pageField; tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"afbc0885430f4042","sum":"G2-L1: never widen restates(); D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live. Guest fixture at x=0; no '--' in .entitlements; say 'at 3pm'; probe an EKEventStore if status flaps. No default chat route (--dev-writer); Gemma drafts few-shot.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fdc428b470104795","sum":"G2-H8: restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule, never widen it; live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial. Guest 960x600: fixture to x=0; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event ⌘Z only after a verified step.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6c27db8da975f9b4","sum":"G2: drafts.ts restates() is a closed clause-suffix rule; looser versions had 5 bypasses, never widen it. Live Jev confirmed Order number but not a reply's To sender or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial (evidence/screen/g2).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6064b9b210ca22b7","sum":"H8: guest is 960x600 pt, move a centred caret-fixture to x=0 or event cards find noClearSpot; seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd; no '--' in .entitlements comments; event card ⌘Z only after a verified step; calendar adds report written:0.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-0c929a2ce63bdaff","text":"H8 VM: the rig guest is 960x600 pt; a centred caret-fixture executor window leaves every event-card spot covering a field (noClearSpot): move it to x=0 (fixture-ax move). seed-user-tcc.sh restarts tccd: running it while a TCC prompt is up shows the prompt twice.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182018Z-327bc9cdd4327c33","text":"H8: an XML comment in an .entitlements file must not contain '--' (AMFIUnserializeXML refuses it and codesign fails). The event card's done line takes ⌘Z only after a verified step; the helper reports written:0 for calendar adds.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f5079ae2f5b9473e","sum":"H8-L1: say 'at 3pm' (an open AM/PM makes no event card); EKEventStore status can flap, probe a store. No default chat route; --dev-writer names one. Gemma E2B is a base model (few-shot drafts); deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1c1ae9c575164268","sum":"H8: 'Thursday at 3' makes no event card since D2-03 (say 'at 3pm'); a card with no end asks how long. EKEventStore.authorizationStatus can flap notDetermined after a grant; host and reader probe a store instead.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T182018Z-f0560794b2ec28fa","text":"H8: since D2-03 an event sentence whose time leaves AM/PM open ('Thursday at 3') makes no event card; use 'at 3pm'. onscreen_acceptance.py still types 'at 3'. A card from a time with no end asks how long (30 min first, Tab takes it).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T182023Z-1d9814a513f71781","text":"H8: in a process running when Calendar access was granted, EKEventStore.authorizationStatus flapped notDetermined/fullAccess (VM) while a new store's calendars(for:) read fine; host and reader probe a store when status says notDetermined (no prompt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f38309cb9958372d","sum":"L1: no chat route by default (writer routes null); a developer names groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer. Gemma E2B is a base model, so local drafts are few-shot; caret-local-model needs a grammar; deadlineMs is epoch ms.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-fdcac01d5471b677","text":"L1: Cotypist's Gemma E2B is a base model, so local draft prompts are few-shot documents (writer/local-draft.ts); caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar. localTextRequest.deadlineMs is epoch ms, not a duration.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"00fd5ab66bea54da","sum":"H10-P2: page plans set WindowSel.page; host reads page focus from pageField only; label >80 blocks saved answers. Tests never read GROQ_API_KEY; new Ask makers join oneAnswer; recheckFields drops only failing fields.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"637b36e430ed09a4","sum":"H10-S1: page plans set WindowSel.page (page and reader windows share id and title); host reads page focus only from pageField. labelTooLong (label >80) blocks saved answers; old hosts lost the memory list on the answers doc id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1de8a2f92e9f1531","sum":"H10: a page window and its browser's reader window share bundle id and title, so page plans set WindowSel.page. Chrome shows AX no web content or focus, so the host reads page focus and frames only from pageField (PageFocusSource).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T203747Z-1771ea16bd50b7ed","text":"H10: a page window and the reader's window of the same browser share bundle id and title; plans for a page must set WindowSel.page or they stop as ambiguous.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T203747Z-8582de2538fa78c4","text":"H10: Chrome shows Accessibility no web content and no focused element while a page field has focus (VM probe), so the host reads page focus and frames only from the helper's pageField (PageFocusSource).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4168398783b277b0","sum":"S1: fill throws labelTooLong for a focused label over 80 chars on a page with little prose, so no saved answer there. Hosts before H11 refused the answers doc id and lost the whole memory list; answers.md is listed only to savedAnswers hosts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T204550Z-12e324b0b44784bf","text":"Fill throws labelTooLong when the focused field's label is over 80 chars on a page with little other prose (privacy prose share); saved answers can't be offered there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T204550Z-3e3d4d7a0bdec136","text":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id, losing the whole memory list; the server lists answers.md only to hosts with the savedAnswers capability.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d6e449e5f141c6b0","sum":"P1-P2: tests never read GROQ_API_KEY (no-groq.ts); a new Ask maker joins planAsk's oneAnswer gate; recheckFields drops only a failing field; derived parts keep their line's label as context, else need an equal line.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"796fd5afdca57f46","sum":"P1: no-groq.ts fails any test reading GROQ_API_KEY even if caught (pass env objects). On W4 Greenhouse, recheckFill refused Fill all: a derived Country part needs a line equal to the span for a control with no label context.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-7ef033e31edcf1b4","text":"P1: helper/test/setup/no-groq.ts (vitest setupFiles) fails any test file that reads process.env.GROQ_API_KEY, even if the throw is caught; pass explicit env objects to readKey/writersOnStart in tests.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-d6ebebc54b7a4ea1","text":"P1: on W4's saved Greenhouse pages Fill all is refused whole by recheckFill (offers/fill-popup.ts ~218): Country 'United States' is a derived part of 'Location: Oakland, California, United States (...)', and a control without label context needs a line equal to the span.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"59654fc6f3466291","sum":"P1-P2: the heads maker is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer; a new maker name must join that gate. A derived part carries its line's label as context; recheckFields drops only the failing field; sourceHolds re-derives spans.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-f4ebc7703c97844e","text":"P1: the heads Ask maker (planner/intent-heads.ts) is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer (oneAnswer = makerName !== 'jev': inferredAll, listsAll, confirmScope); a new maker name must be added to that gate or its scope stands unconfirmed.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-519d2cf2c3af807c","text":"P2: a fill part derived from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as FillHandoff.context; recheckFields drops a field that fails its recheck and runs the rest; an unlabelled span inside a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it (fill-popup.ts sourceHolds).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9199063a79210b69","sum":"P2-P4 pages: page-link patches a verified write (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; freeze goldens via zod.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"04e70b9b4b65451f","sum":"P2-C1 pages: page-link patches a written control (one trailing walk); page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (clones refused); CfT calls Google via any proxy; guest Mail has no account; window-left skips the browser's reader window; check undo over CDP; goals leave restored picks.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"c4886c398087e862","sum":"P2-H10: page-link patches a verified write, walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS later; page Asks plan in page-planner.ts (gate 'fill' by identity: clones refused); headless CfT calls Google via any proxy (F1: browserService); guest Mail has no account (.eml: Add Account).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"353d6de786750cc3","sum":"P2: page-link patches a written control and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. A page Ask is planned by page-planner.ts with no writer; gate 'fill' is marked by identity, so propose refuses a structuredClone'd plan.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-878907191e2eb647","text":"P2: engines/page-link.ts no longer walks after a verified pageWrite/pageSelect/pageSetChecked; it patches that control in the tab's last walk and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. Tests that expected a pageWalk after an ok write must expect the patch.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-d4c70d849120ef71","text":"P2: an Ask about a page (goals:true) comes back as AskGoal.page and is planned by goals/page-planner.ts with no writer; its steps are gate 'fill', which only lowering marks (gates.ts markFilled, by identity), so GoalRuns.propose refuses a structuredClone'd page plan.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"dc7a4168ce70092a","sum":"F1-H10: headless CfT calls Google hosts through any proxy; the F1 sink files them as browserService(), not offsite(). The rig guest's Mail has no account (an .eml shows Add Account; its buttons label in AXDescription).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T224055Z-4008dd64a8214ebf","text":"Headless Chrome for Testing keeps calling Google hosts (google.com, googleapis.com) through a proxy whatever flags it gets; the F1 network sink (fixtures/web-form/oracle.ts) files them under browserService(), not offsite().","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T235610Z-e61928d562069b22","text":"H10: in the rig guest Mail has no account: opening an .eml shows the Add Account sheet, not the message; its SwiftUI buttons carry their label in AXDescription, not AXTitle.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2eaf29a830280b84","sum":"H10-C1: a page's window just left skips its browser's reader window; F1's probe lags the DOM (check undo over CDP); 'from my notes' reads one resolved window; goal runs leave a restored combobox pick to the user and skip its dependents.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"62823ecfd9d9074a","sum":"H10-F1: a page's window just left skips its browser's own reader window (else Jev withheld at 0.65-0.77); F1's probe can lag the DOM after a burst of writes, so check undo by reading the DOM over CDP (page-loop-eval DOM_VALUES_JS).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T235611Z-1dede3bef7f49f2e","text":"H10: a page's 'window just left' (ScreenModel.windowBefore) skips the reader's window of the same browser; without that, Jev withheld page fills at 0.65-0.77.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T005116Z-802d1a3e98c70699","text":"F1's probe posts state with fetch keepalive and drops a failed post after recording it sent, so after a burst of writes the oracle can lag the DOM; page-loop-eval checks undo by reading the DOM over CDP (DOM_VALUES_JS).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0a881e10261f1993","sum":"P2-C1: 'from my notes' makes an Ask read only the window it resolves to (a decoy on the corpus); goal runs leaveFailedToYou: a restored combobox pick is listed (Executor.leftToYou) and dependents (state/city/ZIP) skipped; other callers stop.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T005116Z-d31529fbf9335d38","text":"P2 evals: an Ask saying 'from my notes' makes code read only the one window it resolves that to (planner/sources.ts); on the corpus that was a decoy note. Page-loop goal runs ask 'fill out this form', which heads settles as a whole form.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021405Z-957fa1314ab52f39","text":"C1: goal segments run with leaveFailedToYou: a combobox pick the page put back (VerbResult restored) and read back unchanged is listed via Executor.leftToYou and the run goes on, skipping a country's state/city/ZIP (executor/dependents.ts). Other callers still stop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"2dd914a0e2eed67d","sum":"P3-C1: mergeCutWalk keeps unsent nodes; attach rows for goalFiles hosts; carries span pages; says.ts never names Jev; freeze goldens via zod; tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor; CfT tab switch via worker; fill budget load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"777a097740a458a3","sum":"P3: cut walks keep unsent nodes (mergeCutWalk); attach rows only for goalFiles hosts, confirmedFile names its step; a carry lives across pages (carryOn); says.ts never names Jev; freeze golden lines through their zod schema (keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"b3b6ceb345ada2a0","sum":"P3: a cut reader walk keeps prior unsent nodes until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); page goals get attach rows only for a goalFiles host (helper.ts filesFor); confirmedFile names the attach step; rows with no file drop from the run (runs.ts stepMap).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021729Z-2e26e31d9e56986f","text":"P3: a cut reader walk (root null, stats.truncated) keeps every prior node it did not send until a complete walk (model.ts mergeCutWalk); inferring 'passed' nodes from the old order dropped a text area that a moved node jumped ahead of. Pages are still replaced whole.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021733Z-eb34e4009fe61d9d","text":"P3: page goals get attach rows only for a host with goalFiles (helper.ts filesFor; in process via HelperOptions.goalFiles); goalAccept.confirmedFile names the attach step, and rows given no file are dropped from the run (runs.ts stepMap maps executor steps back to segment steps).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b342efa209afe515","sum":"P3: a carry lives across pages until its goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn; pageWalked leaves a carried document alone); says.ts never names Jev ('Caret's model'); freeze golden lines through their zod schema (parse writes keys in schema order).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T021750Z-652b23e48a36082a","text":"P3: a carry lives across pages until a carried goal finishes (runs.ts carryOn); GoalRuns.carrying(windowId, doc) is true only for the document a carry plans, so helper.ts pageWalked leaves that page alone and takes any page the carry planned nothing for.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T021800Z-55351013aa4fbe71","text":"P3: user sentences in planner/says.ts never name Jev (test/says.test.ts plain()); Jev failure sentences say 'Caret's model'. Golden lines must be normalised through their zod schema before freezing: parse writes keys in schema order, so a round trip of a hand-built line differs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"c9f2c23e721be85d","sum":"P4-C1: tab-left text only via TabSource.viewFor(owner), never ScreenModel; CfT tab switches via chrome.tabs/windows.update in the worker (switchTo); fill's 15 ms budget makes probes load-dependent (budgetMs Infinity); line values read in TS (line-values.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"298edb042298a31c","sum":"P4: text read from the tab left never enters ScreenModel; only fill sees it via TabSource.viewFor(owner). Headless CfT tab switches the extension sees: chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the worker over the DevTools pipe (tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032217Z-1ff9070e78c5cbc1","text":"P4: text read from the tab the user just left never enters ScreenModel; only fill paths see it, via TabSource.viewFor(owner) (engines/tab-source.ts). Never hand helper.model views or TabSource nodes to other consumers (router, event cards, shadow, transfers).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032245Z-9aff69e636408257","text":"P4: headless CfT tab switches that the extension's tabs/windows listeners really see: evaluate chrome.tabs.update + chrome.windows.update in the extension worker over the DevTools pipe (fixtures/web-form/tab-source-journey.ts switchTo).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"05ed1f5f8cad4a0d","sum":"C1: fill's candidate budget (15 ms wall clock) makes in-process probes load-dependent (45-62 proposed under load ~30): compare at like load or pass budgetMs Infinity; fill reads values inside lines in TS (line-values.ts); recheck counts code-found ones via lineGives.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T032641Z-108c3beb10547e40","text":"C1: the candidate generator's 15 ms wall-clock budget makes in-process fill probes load-dependent: the corpus probe swung 45-62 proposed under load avg ~30; compare runs only at like load, or pass budgetMs Infinity.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T032641Z-52a641b0527a12b8","text":"C1: fill reads values inside lines in TS (fill/line-values.ts, candidates.ts windowValues), so the page-loop eval's replayed sources (values: []) now get typed values as the reader would give them; the recheck counts only reader values as typed, code-found ones via lineGives.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
